  "claim_short": "The future-work statement after Theorem 6.1 suggests that its kernel hypothesis (6.3) should hold for every nonnegative potential V in RH_q, q>d/2. This packet proves the suggestion under the conventions forced by the source's examples and finite-speed formula: the standard critical radius uses a supremum, H=-Delta+V, and the wave multiplier is psi(sigma sqrt(H)).",
